1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,850
A doctor watches a patient's heartbeat, not just waits for collapse. Watch your app's health all the time.

2
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:15,150
Logs say what happened. Metrics count how much. Uptime checks ask: is it up right now?

3
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:24,575
A runbook says exactly what to do when an alert fires: check this, restart that, call this person.

4
00:00:25,270 --> 00:00:29,445
Health checks, logs, metrics, and a calm, written plan.

5
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:38,750
Alert on what users feel: errors, slowness, downtime. Too many alerts, and people ignore them all.

6
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:44,300
Every alert needs an owner, and a runbook that says what to do.

